              "reviewerRole": "product-manager",
              "actor": "product-manager",
              "verdict": "sendBack",
              "summary": "One defect to fix: lanes do not resolve against declared actors.\n\nDEFECT (Actors and lanes). Every activity diagram, core and nonCore, puts most of its nodes in a swim lane with roleName \"Todo List\". No use case declares an actor with that role. The declared actors are only \"Team Member\" and \"Agent Tool\". Either:\n(a) declare the system lane as an actor on each use case, with a role that matches the lane name exactly, or\n(b) rename the lanes so each roleName matches a declared actor, and keep system behavior in a lane that is declared.\nPick one convention and apply it to all 11 use cases.\n\nRelated, same fix pass: \"Agent Tool\" is declared as an actor on both core use cases but never appears in any lane or node. Either give it a lane, for example where an agent states a change or reads the list, or drop it from the actors. The essence rationales lean on the agent-tool surface to show the client-surface volatility is exercised, so I'd keep it and show it in the flows.\n\nEverything else passes:\n- Count: 2 cores, within range.\n- Rejection trail: all 9 nonCore use cases have reasons, and each variationOf resolves to a core id.\n- Essence: both rationales argue the use case is shared, durable and differentiating.\n- No channel-shaped use cases.\n- Volatility exercise: the rationales name client surface, access-protocol revision and storage technology. The .volatilities slot is not committed, so I checked this against the three names in the rationales and the earlier volatilities commit, not against the committed slot.\n- Abstraction: nine raw use cases collapse under two named abstractions.\n\nReservations on the approve path, taste-level only, not grounds for revise:\n- \"Revise the commitments\" comes close to a CRUD umbrella (add, edit, remove, toggle). I accept it because the rationale frames it as one business act, changing the set of commitments. Keep the wording business-shaped in later artifacts.\n- The nonCore flows list only Team Member. That is fine as variations, but it would be more consistent if Agent Tool were acknowledged.",
